{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Then.</b> When He gave Israel the well, they sang; and this song was not mentioned at the time of the event, because on its account Moses and Aaron were punished. When he came to mention the well, he also mentioned the song. Another interpretation: <b>In the book of the wars of YHWH</b> — like the book of Chronicles, in which they would record the wars and victories between nation and nation." "<b>Et Vahev.</b> One word, and it is like אתיהב, the vav interchanging with yod — like בהתודע יוסף, which is from ידע; הוה גביר like היה; and it is an expression of giving — like כי לא נתן להם נחלה, which is translated הרי לא אתיהב להון אחסנא. And so it is written in the book: <b>את והב בסופה</b> — that is, the king of Moab gave בסופה ובסערה, and he was victorious." "<b>And the streams of Arnon.</b> And with the streams he was victorious, for Sihon took all his land as far as the stream of Arnon. <b>And from there the well.</b> From that slope of the streams — and from their journeys the well would flow forth and go out from the rock."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {1 "The phrase את והב בסופה is read as 'he gave Vahev at Suphah'; the argument turns on reading את as 'gave' (Aramaic אתיהב) with vav-yod interchange."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:08.194172421Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}